  "id": "pattern-discrimination",
  "term": "pattern discrimination",
  "definition": "Pattern discrimination is the ability to detect differences between patterns in what is heard. In this source, it refers specifically to telling apart different lexical stress patterns, with performance varying by a person’s language background and dominance.",
